course: dictionary
lesson: 14027
title: Malice and the wish to hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Malice means a wish to hurt someone, or to make bad things happen to them. It is a feeling you have inside, and you choose to act on it. «Mia pushed the boy into the puddle with malice.» She did it on purpose because she wanted him to be hurt, so the phrase with malice tells you her reason was cruel.
explain: Context gives you clues. Look at the words around malice: a deliberate act, a plan, a villain who wants trouble. «The wicked queen spread lies out of pure malice.» The phrase out of malice tells you the reason was a wish to hurt others.
explain: Malice is not the same as a mistake. «Sam knocked over the paint by accident, without malice.» Without malice means he did not want to hurt anyone, so it was an accident, not a cruel act. A mistake can be sorry, but it is not malice.
fact: Malice is a noun, a name for a feeling or a wish.
fact: «Malice» means the wish to hurt someone or make bad things happen to them.
fact: In law, «malice» means the intention to do harm when breaking the law.
fact: Useful phrases: «with malice», «out of malice», and «without malice».
fact: In stories, malice often marks a villain, and it separates a mistake from a cruel act done on purpose.
exercise: «The thief broke the window out of malice, because he wanted the shop owner to suffer.» What does malice mean here? | A wet day at the market | *A wish to hurt someone | A kind plan to help the shop owner | A loud noise in the street
exercise: «Ella dropped the cake by accident, and she had no malice at all.» What does «no malice» tell us? | She was very hungry | *She did not mean to hurt anyone | She was lost on the way home | She wanted to hurt the baker
exercise: Which word means a wish to hurt someone? | Patience | Laughter | Kindness | *Malice
test: «The villain smiled with malice as he planned his trap.» Malice in this sentence means | Being very tired | Friendship | A sweet taste | *Wanting to hurt someone
test: A judge asks if the man broke the law with malice. In law, what does malice mean? | Being very late for court | Telling a funny joke | Carrying a heavy bag | *The intention to do harm when breaking the law
exam: «He broke the vase without malice, and he said sorry at once.» What is the best meaning of without malice? | He was angry with his family | He wanted to hurt the vase | *He did not want to hurt anyone | He was fast asleep
